2.2 Reconciliation Engine
Responsibilities: Consume from tx.orders.* and tx.payments.*, perform windowed matching, write results to
PostgreSQL, publish unmatched events to recon.failures.*.
Idempotency design: Before processing any event, the engine executes Redis SETNX
reconguard:idem:{tenantId}:{msgId} 1 EX 86400. If the key already exists, the event is a duplicate and is ACK'd
without reprocessing.
Windowing: The 30-second tumbling window is stored in Redis as a HASH keyed by {tenantId}:{transactionId} with a
TTL of 35 seconds (5s grace).
Matching Tolerance Rules
• Amounts: within ±0.02 of the base currency unit (configurable per tenant).
• Timestamps: order event and payment event within ±120 seconds.
• Currency: normalized to order's base currency using cached FX rate (refreshed every 60s).
