Security Measures
• PII masking in logs: A Logback MaskingConverter replaces card numbers, IBANs, and email addresses with
[MASKED] before any log appender writes.
• Data encryption: All PostgreSQL connections use TLS 1.3. The pg_encrypt extension encrypts raw_context
JSONB at rest for opted-in tenants. Redis connections use TLS + AUTH.
• Idempotency keys: All write endpoints require X-Idempotency-Key: . Stored in Redis with 24-hour TTL. Duplicate
requests return the cached response.
